<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chilean Civil Code</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1855</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Chilean Civil Code, drafted by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andres-bello">Andrés Bello</a> and promulgated in December 1855, came into force in 1857. Drawing on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-law">Roman law</a>, Spanish legislation and the French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleonic-code">Napoleonic Code</a>, it regulated persons, property, contracts and inheritance in clear, systematic language. It was adopted almost unchanged by Ecuador and Colombia and influenced the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/civil-law">civil law</a> of several other <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> American countries.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chilean-civil-code.jpg" alt="Chilean Civil Code" width="288" height="466" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Codigo_Civil_Chile_01.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
